Instructions for Creating an Executable File in Java type from MacOS.

Step 1: Compile the main class used.
• Navigate to the project root. (FIT3077Santorini in my case).
• Run the code
javac -d out -cp src src/prototype/pee_yee_peen/Application.java
• The compiled file will now be compiled and stored in the ‘out’ directory.

Step 2: Create a JAR File
• Run the code.
jar cfe FIT3077Santorini.jar prototype.pee_yee_peen.Application -C out .

Step 3: Check the functionality of the JAR file.
• Run the code
java -jar FIT3077Santorini.jar

Step 4: Use jpackage to pack the ‘.jar’ file into an ‘.app’ file
• Run the chunk of code below.
jpackage --name FIT3077Santorini \
--input out \
--main-jar FIT3077Santorini.jar \
--main-class prototype.pee_yee_peen.Application \
--type app-image